  "id": "cortical-activation",
  "term": "cortical activation",
  "definition": "Cortical activation is the level of activity in areas of the brain’s cortex while a person performs a task. In this context, it refers to task-related activity in regions such as the prefrontal and vestibular cortices, estimated from changes in oxygenated blood, and lower activation after practice may reflect more efficient cognitive-motor processing.",
